---- the_logic_crates_carry_no_unnamed_guest_os_assumption stdout ----

thread 'the_logic_crates_carry_no_unnamed_guest_os_assumption' (1676626) panicked at tests/tests/guest_os_axis_gate.rs:368:5:
★ AN OS ASSUMPTION WITH NO COMMENT NAMING IT — `four_axes_of_variation.md` §5 rule 3.

  crates/kayfabe-abi/src/submit.rs:5095  [/dev/]  /dev/nvidiactl or /dev/nvidia0 across all six host_reference_ga106 \

The guest OS is the fourth axis, and it is UNDETECTABLE ON THE WIRE: it is a
build flag in the guest driver, not a protocol field. So a line that assumes it
cannot be checked by anything at runtime — the only defence is that it says so.

Two ways out, and picking one is a design decision:
- the assumption is REAL -> put it behind `kayfabe_abi::GuestOs`, where the arm
for an OS we have no rule for is a typed refusal;
- the assumption is INCIDENTAL -> say so in a comment naming the OS, within 40 lines above the line.

This gate exists because on 2026-07-29 the answer was neither: `client_kind_from_process_id` applied a UNIX-only rule to every guest and folded the guest kernel's RM clients in with a guest process's.
note: run with `RUST_BACKTRACE=1` environment variable to display a backtrace


